4. TEACH ORDER OF OPERATIONS CORRECTLY
========================================================

When a lesson teaches PEMDAS or order of operations, the instructional explanation must accurately communicate the hierarchy.

Use this sequence:

1. Grouping symbols: work from the innermost grouping outward.
2. Exponents.
3. Multiplication and division, working from left to right.
4. Addition and subtraction, working from left to right.

Explicitly teach that multiplication does not automatically come before division, and addition does not automatically come before subtraction.

When appropriate, use the term PEMDAS, but explain its meaning accurately.

Do not present a misleading rule that encourages students to perform all multiplication before division or all addition before subtraction.

Every worked example must demonstrate the correct hierarchy.

Include explanations of why each operation is performed at that stage.

